WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.580
13.8 billion dollars is the deficit bc's three main leaders debated Wednesday. This is vancouver

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:13.480
daily, episode 23. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. I don't live in vancouver. David

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.880
eby, Lauren Dorkson and Emily Lowen spent almost two hours Wednesday night in downtown vancouver.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.500
Shachie Curl, who leads the Angus Reed Institute, moderated the only televised debate before

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.640
for the October 24th election, the Vancouver Sun Reports.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.980
Male ballots have to arrive by October 17th.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.400
EBS said a one-seat majority becomes a tie once a speaker

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.000
is appointed, so any vote could topple the government.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.180
He said families need bigger moves and representatives

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.800
from every part of the province focused on priorities

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.960
rather than culture wars or repealing the human rights code.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.640
Dorkson, the conservative interim leader, said the campaign

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.760
is about EBS decade in the legislature

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.960
and that nothing is better than years ago.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:59.020
He promised respect and dignity, said he will expect that from his caucus, and told City

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.440
News he will not table a platform he then breaks.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:06.680
Lowen, the youngest leader on stage, and the only woman there, said she rents and has worked

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:07.500
for minimum wage.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.980
She said green priorities are the cost of living and climate, through sustainability

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.560
and local economic growth.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:18.220
If her party held the balance of power, she said proportional representation would be her

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:18.780
first fight.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:24.240
EB tied hospital and school building to the red ink and said he would go after wasteful spending.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:29.320
He said the books can be balanced without loading the cost onto residents. His plan would tax

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:36.260
income above $190,000 and pause the 10 cent a liter fuel tax for a time. He attacked a conservative

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:42.170
proposal to lift the income tax threshold to $32,000. A change some economists say could cost

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.070
up to $4 billion.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:49.910
Dorkson wants that tax change, LNG output tripled by 2035, fewer rules, and a temporary

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:53.030
end to the 10% provincial sales tax on Canadian liquor.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.370
He also wants support for forestry.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.110
He criticized a $1,000 rebate that was offered and then pulled.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:04.050
Low-and-set extraction is getting the money without a sustainable path, and she wants value

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:07.490
added local industry plus a tax on ultra-wealthy households.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:12.050
EBS said thousands of daycare spaces have opened and that more are still needed.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.070
Low and said family doctor promises have not been met.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:18.630
EBS answered with recruitment and the age of the population ahead.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.490
On car insurance, Dorxon wants a hybrid instead of no fault.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:27.150
EBS said bringing personal injury lawyers back is what drained ICBC before.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.330
EBS restated partnership with indigenous communities.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:34.730
Dorxon said he would repeal the Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples Act

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.870
because he believes it has divided people.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:40.810
Lowen said the task is to carry that act out, not take it apart.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:46.270
Dorkson was pressed on reposts by campaign manager Katie Marifield, including lines calling

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:51.430
Islam a literal rape culture, and calling New York mayor Zaron Momdani a jihadi-loving

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:51.710
mayor.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:56.950
He said she was responding to events in the UK as a sexual assault survivor, apologized,

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.030
deleted the posts, and will remain.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:03.830
He has already dropped one candidate over a post-amed at pro-Palestinian protesters.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:08.830
Ebi said parts of her feed read like the worst corners of the dark web against a call

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:12.290
from national Muslim organizations that people need to feel safe here.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:17.710
Lowen called the clash a rerun of 2024, with conservatives split by candidates' comments

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.410
and what she termed a managed decline under Ebi.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:25.510
Asked about governing with the conservatives to avoid another election, Ebi said he struggles

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:30.210
to find shared ground that he is not perfect and that he will act for British Columbians.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:35.530
In video remarks, center BC's Eleanor Sturco said she is not asking anyone to pretend

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:36.930
her party will form government.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:41.710
She asked who will hold the next government to account and described center BC as socially

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:45.370
progressive, environmentally pragmatic, and fiscally responsible.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:51.850
One BC's Dallas Brody, also on video, said she will push a 25% income tax cut for people

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:56.910
in corporations, a 2% sales tax cut, and a fight against what she called land back

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:02.692
giveaways and the reconciliation industry. Burnaby schools say the September 21st

00:04:02.692 --> 00:04:07.052
ransomware attack reached websites, portals, internal networks, and phone lines.

00:04:07.512 --> 00:04:11.472
The Globe and Mail reports the district's notice says copied files may list parent,

00:04:11.932 --> 00:04:16.652
guardian, and student names in contacts, along with birth dates, grades, and school names.

00:04:17.172 --> 00:04:21.732
Those files may also hold registration forms, Kindergarten assessment notes, and lists of

00:04:21.732 --> 00:04:27.032
students on specialized learning plans. CBC says the district now includes identifying documents

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:33.212
and medical information. Medical diagnoses among them. The RCMP and the Provincial Privacy Commissioner

00:04:33.212 --> 00:04:38.512
have the file. Security is under review and families can register for a Trans Union fraud alert.

00:04:38.952 --> 00:04:43.312
The district is telling people to watch for odd messages and says updates will follow the

00:04:43.312 --> 00:04:49.493
investigation. The BC Lumber Trade Council told CBC the combined American duty on softwood

00:04:49.493 --> 00:04:55.123
exports is now almost 35 percent. That is down from the 45 percent combined rate announced in

00:04:55.123 --> 00:05:00.723
August last year. A Washington state grand jury has indicted James Bryant, who is 30, as

00:05:00.723 --> 00:05:03.563
an alleged co-conspirator in the Tumblr Ridge mass shooting.

00:05:04.223 --> 00:05:09.243
CBC says the charge is conspiracy to murder persons in a foreign country, which gives prosecutors

00:05:09.243 --> 00:05:15.702
probable cause to proceed. He is accused. He has not been convicted. A 64-year-old woman

00:05:15.702 --> 00:05:20.182
has died from injuries in the September 30th crash at Suwassen Mills, the Vancouver

00:05:20.182 --> 00:05:25.142
Sun reports. She is the third person killed in that crash. Delta police are still on the

00:05:25.142 --> 00:05:30.162
investigation. Parkboard Chair Tom Digby told Global News the Vancouver Aquatic Center

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:35.222
cannot come back as a 50-meter pool because land claims are unsettled. He chaired the board

00:05:35.222 --> 00:05:39.942
when it chose demolition, and he is running again as a Vancouver Green. The board has said

00:05:39.942 --> 00:05:43.942
a 50-meter pool needs a bigger footprint for current safety and competition rules.

00:05:44.622 --> 00:05:49.062
Digby said the province owns the foreshore and will not allow the expansion until claims are settled.

00:05:49.662 --> 00:05:54.862
Musqueam Chief Wayne Sparrow said a letter went to MST Development Corporation. The Musqueam,

00:05:54.862 --> 00:06:00.042
Squamish and Slay-Watuth partnership, seeking a lease to the city. He said the proposed rent

00:06:00.042 --> 00:06:05.402
was as little as $1, and asked what accommodation that leaves his nation. No meeting has happened

00:06:05.402 --> 00:06:10.562
yet. He said one still could. An injunction for protecting our Vancouver Aquatic Center holds

00:06:10.562 --> 00:06:15.222
demolition until at least November 3rd, the day after the first scheduled park board meeting.

00:06:15.802 --> 00:06:20.802
John Gerard, the group's director and a team park board candidate, said a rebuild still has to

00:06:20.802 --> 00:06:26.449
